From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:11:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: google: gs101-pmu: describe the CLKOUT pads

The gs201 PMU node describes its CLKOUT pads as clock outputs
(#clock-cells, the TCXO as the CLKOUT mux's input 0), which the
exynos-clkout driver binds to provide the Pixel 7 Pro's NFC reference
clock. The binding didn't allow those properties, so dtbs_check flagged
the node on gs201-cheetah.

Allow #clock-cells, one input clock and its "clkout0" name, as
samsung,exynos-pmu.yaml does for the Exynos PMUs.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/soc/google/google,gs101-pmu.yaml     | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/google/google,gs101-pmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/google/google,gs101-pmu.yaml
index b88a04ae3..77be28079 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/google/google,gs101-pmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/google/google,gs101-pmu.yaml
@@ -28,6 +28,21 @@ properties:
 
   ranges: true
 
+  "#clock-cells":
+    const: 1
+    description:
+      The PMU's CLKOUT pads (PAD_CTRL_CLKOUTn), one clock each, which
+      drive the PMU's selected input out to a board device.
+
+  clocks:
+    description:
+      The input the CLKOUT pads select, the TCXO on gs201.
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clock-names:
+    items:
+      - const: clkout0
+
   reboot-mode:
     $ref: /schemas/power/reset/syscon-reboot-mode.yaml
     type: object
